- **mpg**: Combined MPG figures for the 2020 Q7 3.0 TDI V6 (50 TDI) are around 33.2-44.1 mpg (Imperial), which translates to roughly 27.6-36.7 mpg (US). EPA combined is around 18 mpg for the petrol V6, but the diesel is more efficient. Real-world diesel figures are often lower than official ratings but still generally good for a large SUV. This is around or above the average 30 mpg.
